From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luan Luciano <luanluciano93@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:18:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lugwave: recover() na goroutine do guarda do #50
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

O #50 sobe uma goroutine por ack de erro (guardAcceptErrorAck), que espera
6 s e pode encerrar a chamada. Ela ganha o mesmo defer e.recoverMedia das
outras goroutines de uma chamada (0006): um panic ali loga com a pilha e
encerra a chamada, em vez de derrubar o processo e com ele todas as
conexões do whatsmeow.

Sai junto com o 0010 (quando o upstream mergear o #50), ou antes, se o
upstream ganhar recover equivalente.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 engine.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/engine.go b/engine.go
index c6a3d71..83a648a 100644
--- a/engine.go
+++ b/engine.go
@@ -890,6 +890,7 @@ func (e *engine) acceptGoneOut(m *engineCall) bool {
 // guardAcceptErrorAck ends a call kept after an error ack on its <accept> when no
 // inbound audio has arrived since the ack: the accept did not land after all.
 func (e *engine) guardAcceptErrorAck(callID string, m *engineCall, errCode string, ackAt time.Time) {
+	defer e.recoverMedia("accept error-ack guard", callID)
 	time.Sleep(acceptErrorAckGrace)
 	if e.lookup(callID) != m {
 		return // already ended (or replaced)
